{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i -e 'P52|coherent-local-hyperbolic|aristotle.*closeout|quarantine' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -80 && sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && pwd && git status --short && rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'PLAN.md' -g 'TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md' -g '*HANDOFF*' -g '*STATUS*' -g 'P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates.md' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"51:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n57:## Task 2: diagnose systemd and quarantine-closeout failures\n61:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, partial: recovered closeout path; FF15/P37 advancement unverified)\n65:- systemd, `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN`, `<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`, `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'`, quarantine snapshot, `.lake`, `lake build`, state.json\n75:- The live runner is `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle_autopilot.py`, configured by `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`. It has independent finite-fiber FF15–FF23 and stabilizer-hyperfinite P37–P46 queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only at terminal status, and advancement only after both machine-readable acceptance and decision fields. [Task 1]\n78:- Persist closeout metadata in `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` before starting Codex. An interrupted closeout without a machine-readable decision halts for review rather than retrying or advancing ambiguously. [Task 2]\n83:- symptom: a closeout consumes about 13 GB and clones/builds Mathlib -> cause: `lake build` was run in a stripped downloaded Aristotle quarantine snapshot with no `.lake` -> fix: inspect/quarantine there, copy only the reviewed candidate to the already-built live project, and run all Lean checks only in that live checkout. [Task 2]\n---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\nlean/stabilizer\n M AGENTS.md\n M Formalization.lean\n M PROGRESS.md\n M README.md\n M aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md\n?? AristotleCandidates/AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/BicommutantNormalTransport.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/BicommutantVonNeumannCore.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarAlphaGNSBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarCompletionAlphaInterface.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarGNSBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/ConcreteCStarCompletion.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/ConstructedAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarEquiv.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateEquivCoherence.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateFactorization.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateMapNormControl.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteProductStateCoherence.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteStabilizerProductState.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/InfiniteAlgebraicRegionalEquiv.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/InfiniteAlgebraicStateTransport.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/NormalVonNeumannExtensionInterface.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/ProductFactorClassificationBoundary.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StatePreservingGNSModel.lean\n?? Formalization/Infrastructure.lean\n?? Formalization/Legacy.lean\n?? Formalization/Manuscript.lean\n?? Formalization/Manuscript/\n?? PLAN.md\n?? aristotle_responses/\n?? aristotle_tasks/P17-finite-stabilizer-product-state.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P18-finite-coordinate-factorization.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P19-cstar-gns-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P20-finite-stabilizer-projector-expectation.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P21-one-qubit-positive-gns-data.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P22-finite-product-gns.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P23-infinite-algebraic-regional-equivalence.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P24-infinite-algebraic-state-transport.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P25-cstar-completion-alpha-interface.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P26-cstar-alpha-gns-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P27-normal-von-neumann-extension-interface.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P28-product-factor-trace-dichotomy.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P29-finite-adapted-coordinate-star-equivalence.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P30-finite-coordinate-equivalence-coherence.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P31-constructed-algebraic-alpha.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P32-finite-product-state-coherence.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P33-cstar-inductive-limit-feasibility.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P34-finite-map-norm-control.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P35-concrete-cstar-completion.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P36-bicommutant-von-neumann-core.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P38-concrete-quasilocal-cstar-model.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P39-state-preserving-gns-model.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P40-bicommutant-normal-transport.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P41-product-factor-classification-boundary.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P42-regional-theorem-contract-audit.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P43-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P44-regional-product-state-and-cstar-model.md\n